  "summary": "DIR-063 COMPLETE - both unfulfilled DIR-060/061 deliverables closed, no self-certification. DELIVERABLE 1 (PDF-vs-DOCX parity): docx-parity.test.js passed 20/20 but was STRUCTURAL ONLY (zip magic, HTML leak, primary colour, native bullets, content tokens, layout table) - the directives real claims were never asserted. Added 5 contracts: section ORDER (anchored on CONTENT, not headings, because Cv4/Cv10 emit no CONTACT/EMPLOYMENT heading and Cv40 matched no synonym - I re-anchored rather than weaken the test), TYPOGRAPHY (name w:sz strictly greater than every heading size, all 51), BULLET INDENT (w:numPr present AND numbering.xml defines a real w:ind), DATES (Jan 2021..Present range survives), CONTACT parity (email+phone+website values survive; the PDF uses ICONS which Word cannot render so the DOCX carries values - documented in the test, not hidden). Result 38/38 (was 33). DELIVERABLE 2 (55-template A4 print/overflow): PROVEN COVERAGE GAP - TEMPLATE_IDS was Array.from({length:51}) so print-probe and overflow-probe NEVER tested a cover, AND main.jsx validated ?template= against TEMPLATE_IDS so ?template=Cover1 SILENTLY FELL BACK TO Cv1 (the probes would have measured Cv1 while reporting a cover). Both probes also required an external LAB_BASE:3000 server and a Linux Chromium at /tmp/chromium-bin, neither of which exists here - so the 55-template verification HAD NEVER RUN AT ALL. Added COVER_TEMPLATE_IDS (Cover1..Cover4, mirroring src/utils/templateRegistry.js) + ALL_TEMPLATE_IDS(55), leaving TEMPLATE_IDS at 51 so the certified 51-entry visual baseline is untouched. NEW template-lab/run-probes.mjs starts vite IN-PROCESS via createServer (same pattern as visual-regression.mjs) so no detached server is spawned and the XAMPP invariant holds, and auto-detects the Playwright Chromium. THREE BUGS FOUND AND FIXED: (1) the first runner used execFileSync which BLOCKS the event loop hosting the in-process vite server, so every navigation deadlocked with page.goto Timeout - fixed with async execFile; (2) vite cold-start pre-bundling exceeded the probe timeout - added a warm-up fetch and raised it to 60s; (3) the print probe reported doc-padding/header-hidden/footer-hidden for every cover - three FALSE failures each, because covers have no .smart-resume-document/.smart-header/.smart-page-footer - now gated behind hasShell while A4 geometry is still asserted for all 55. RESULTS (executed): overflow minimal/long/extreme = 0/55 clip visible content and 0/55 waste >12%; print long = 55/55 pass; Cover1..Cover4 confirmed 794x1123 A4 with 0px cut in every run. GATES: new dir063 suite 6/6; backend docx suites 38/38; test:product exit 0; test:security:static exit 0; lint 0 errors; build exit 0 in 2.55s; INV-1 src/cv-templates ZERO DIFF vs e314f715. HONEST LIMITS: NO true pixel-level DOCX-vs-PDF comparison - that needs a DOCX renderer; LibreOffice 26.8.1.1 was installed this session but is NOT yet wired into the parity harness, so I am NOT claiming visual parity. Covers are not composed so have no pagination to sever. Fixtures not live candidate data. I ran print at 1 fixture and overflow at 3, not the full 9-fixture x 2-probe matrix (~990 page loads). Doc: .bridge/evidence/dir063-implementation-evidence.md"
